   "html": "A student investigates the resistance of a light-dependent resistor (LDR). The resistance of an LDR changes as the intensity of light falling on it varies. The resistance <i>R</i> of the LDR is calculated using the equation <i>R</i> = \\(\\frac{<i>V</i>}{<i>I</i>}\\) where <i>V</i> is the potential difference (p.d.) across the LDR and <i>I</i> is the current in the LDR. Plan an experiment to investigate how the light intensity affects the resistance of an LDR. You are <b>not</b> required to carry out the experiment. The apparatus available includes:",
